<title>USA: Gensia unit gets ANDA nod for cancer drug.</title>
<headline>Gensia unit gets ANDA nod for cancer drug.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gensia Sicor Inc said on Monday that its subsidiary Gensia Laboratories Ltd received U.S. Food and Drug Administration approval on a supplemental Abbreviated New Drug Application (ANDA) for its etoposide injection in a 50 ml multiple dose polymer vial.</p>
<p>Etoposide is a chemotherapeutic agent used to treat patients with small cell lung cancer and refractory testicular tumors.</p>
<p>Gensia Laboratories develops products for use in oncology and other key specialty pharmaceuticals in anesthesiology and cardiology.</p>
</text>
